// v3358 -- THE PERCEPTUAL METRICS MEET EXACT GROUND TRUTH, AND FIND SOMETHING.
//
// The phantom in physics/tomography is CONSTRUCTED from ellipses rather than measured, so unlike every other
// image comparison in this tree there is a right answer -- which is why this is where a perceptual threshold
// could finally be EARNED instead of borrowed from img2threejs or deferred waiting for a rig.
//
// *** scoreRecon IS AFFINE-INVARIANT BY CONSTRUCTION, AND REPORTS A PERFECT SCORE FOR A WRONG PICTURE. ***
//     recon = truth * 1.3  ->  corr 1.0000000000000522, rms 9.9e-14
//     recon = truth + 0.4  ->  corr 1.0000000000000740, rms 2.9e-13
// Both "perfect". This is NOT an undiscovered defect: ct.js states it chose scale-invariance "since the filter
// fixes an arbitrary gain", and for asking whether the ramp filter worked that is the right choice. It is the
// wrong choice for asking whether the reconstruction is CORRECT -- and for CT that matters more than anywhere
// else, because the absolute attenuation IS the diagnostic content. The tree only had the first question.
//
// *** THE FINDING: FBP RECONSTRUCTS AT A GAIN OF 0.649, AND MORE DATA DOES NOT FIX IT. *** Stable to 0.4% across
// a FOURFOLD change in angle count (0.65307 at 64 angles, 0.64906 at 256), so it is a normalisation constant and
// not a convergence failure -- a convergence problem shrinks with data and this does not. Removing the fitted
// gain and offset drops the absolute error from 0.451 to 0.145: the residual correlation hides is dominated by
// ONE CONSTANT, which is a fixable thing rather than a fact of life. Correlation could never have said so,
// because dividing that constant out is precisely what it does.
//   WHETHER TO CORRECT IT IS A DECISION AND NOT A FIX. The device deliberately accommodates the gain, so changing
//   the filter changes what the device CLAIMS. Logged as OPEN in tools/ship/nextRounds.mjs for whoever owns it.
//
// THE FIRST EARNED PERCEPTUAL THRESHOLD IN THIS TREE. At 8 angles edge overlap reads 0.2234 while correlation
// still reads 0.7528 -- streaks from too few projections destroy the linework long before they move a pixel-wise
// score. At 256 angles edges reach 0.9666. Any threshold in 0.5..0.9 separates them, measured against exact
// ground truth rather than imported from a photograph of a knife.
//
// AND AN HONEST NEGATIVE, worth as much as the positives: pHash is the WEAKEST signal here, moving at most 4 bits
// of 63 across the entire sweep, because an 8x8 DCT signature cannot tell a streaked blob from a clean one. It
// earns its place on browser screenshots and not on tomography, and that is recorded rather than quietly dropped.
//
// THE SHARED WINDOW IS LOAD-BEARING: windowing each image by its OWN range makes the 30%-too-bright case
// PIXEL-IDENTICAL -- zero pixels differ -- reproducing the exact blindness this instrument exists to remove.
//
// ---- TWO PIECES OF HOUSEKEEPING THAT ARE NOT HOUSEKEEPING ----
//
// FOUR PAGES MOVED INTO ARRIVING, ON PURPOSE. hmc-bench, ising-bench, magmap-bench and consistency-fleet sat in
// drawers, which is where a page goes when it is FINISHED. They are not finished: each exists to produce a report
// from real hardware and none ever has. A drawer is where a page goes to be found once; ARRIVING IS WHERE IT
// STAYS UNTIL SOMEBODY ACTS ON IT, which is the right shelf for an open obligation. Each carries its reason and
// the submission kind that settles it, and moves to a drawer the day its verdict lands.
//
// AND A STANDING BACKLOG THAT IS NOT PROSE (tools/ship/nextRounds.mjs). v3314 audited fifteen "its own round"
