// v3395 -- THE PERSISTENT SKILLBOOK. The idea is ACE's; the dependency is refused and the scope is narrower.
//
// ACE (kayba-ai/agentic-context-engine, implementing arXiv 2510.04618, Stanford/SambaNova) puts three roles round
// a persistent Skillbook: an Agent executes, a Reflector mines traces for what worked, a SkillManager adds,
// refines and removes strategies. uv, LiteLLM, an API key and a hosted product all fail this tree's bar for
// adoption, so the IDEA is taken and NONE OF THE CODE IS.
//
// THE ROUNDHOUSE ALREADY HAD TWO OF THE THREE ROLES, AND ONE OF THEM IS BETTER THAN THE PAPER'S. roleDecompose is
// propose/critique/revise ending in a real gate. deviceCritic is a DETERMINISTIC critic -- it cannot hallucinate,
// cannot rate-limit, cannot be charged for, and it names the exact defect from a fixed list. ACE's Reflector
// INFERS what worked from traces with no ground truth, which is the inference-versus-knowing split this tree has
// declined three times. What was genuinely missing was persistence: every critique the roundhouse produced died
// with its session.
//
// *** THE SCOPE IS NARROWER THAN ACE'S ON PURPOSE, AND THAT IS WHAT MAKES IT HONEST. *** modelBench already drew
// the line, before this existed:
//     MALFORMED  -- no observable, an unknown observable, no comparator, a target with no tol. AN INTERFACE
//                   FAILURE. A hint can fix it, and the critic names which one it was.
//     REFUSED    -- a WELL-FORMED claim the physics rejected. modelBench's own words: "only a better model fixes
//                   this". NO STRATEGY CAN FIX THIS, and a book that mined it would be teaching a model to guess
//                   luckier, which is not a skill and cannot be verified.
// So a strategy triggers on one of five MALFORMED reasons and nothing else. Constructing one on an invented
// trigger THROWS, and an issue the mapper does not recognise yields NO strategy rather than a guess -- which is
// how a REFUSED can never become a trigger by accident.
//
// *** AND A STRATEGY IS NEVER INJECTED UNTIL A TWO-ARM TRIAL MEASURES IT CHANGING THE OUTCOME. *** The control
// arm is the thing ACE has not got: a Reflector mining "what worked" sees only the runs that happened, so if the
// model improved on its own between Tuesday and Thursday, the strategy added on Wednesday takes the credit and
// nothing in the design can tell that apart from the strategy working. Both arms run the same questions in the
// same session, and it costs one extra run.
//   MEASURED: a hint dropping the rate 0.650 -> 0.050 over 40 questions is PROVEN. An identical-arm hint
//   (0.650 -> 0.650) is RETIRED AND KEPT WITH ITS NUMBERS, because "we tried this and it did nothing" is a result
//   the next person should not have to rediscover. And 0.900 -> 0.100 measured on FOUR trials is still PROPOSED,
//   because four runs is a rumour however good the ratio looks.
//
// STATE IS DERIVED ON LOAD, NEVER READ FROM DISK -- the licence ratchet from physics/proposers.mjs, applied to
// strategies. Hand-editing "state": "proven" into the JSON buys nothing: the file re-derives from the evidence
// attached and NAMES the override, so the edit is visible rather than merely ineffective. There is no state in
// which an unmeasured strategy reaches a prompt.
//
// THE SHIPPED BOOK IS EMPTY, AND SAYS SO. ACE ships with strategies mined from someone else's traces. A strategy
// that has not been trialled on THIS tree's devices has no evidence here, and evidence is the only thing that
// lets one be used. The book fills on a rig, or it stays empty and honest.
//
// Registry 63 -> 64. Knowledge index 737 -> 738 gates.
