// v3408 -- WAVEGUIDE CUTOFFS, WHERE THE BOUNDARY CONDITION IS THE PHYSICS. Plus front doors, six of nine.
//
// A hollow metal pipe carries NOTHING below its cutoff and a discrete set of modes above it, both from one 2D
// eigenproblem with the exact answer kc = pi sqrt((m/a)^2 + (n/b)^2).
//
// *** TE AND TM ARE THE SAME PROBLEM WITH A DIFFERENT BOUNDARY CONDITION, AND THAT DIFFERENCE DECIDES WHICH MODE
// IS DOMINANT. *** Ez must vanish on a conductor (Dirichlet, so TM needs both indices at least one -- THERE IS NO
// TM10) while Hz has a vanishing normal derivative (Neumann, so TE allows a zero index, and TE10 is the mode
// every rectangular guide is designed around). Solve TM with the Neumann operator and it returns 1.5702 instead
// of 3.5081: that is TE10, A MODE TM DOES NOT HAVE. A tidy, plausible cutoff for a pipe that does not exist --
// which is exactly why the MODE SET is gated and not only the frequencies, since the frequencies look fine.
//
// MEASURED: TE10 reaches pi/a to 4.0e-4 at nx=32 with the error falling as h^2 (2.25 and 1.78 for grid ratios
// 1.5 and 1.333); TM11/TE10 comes out 2.23425 against sqrt(5); and TE01/TE20 are DEGENERATE for a 2:1 guide to
// 9.7e-14 -- nothing in the matrix knows they should be, it falls out of the geometry. The Neumann problem
// carries exactly one ZERO eigenvalue at -8e-13, dropped BY NAME because a constant has no curvature, not by a
// tolerance because it happens to be small.
//
// THE SOLVER DOES NOT KNOW THE ANSWER SEPARATES. A rectangle's eigenvalues split into an x part and a y part and
// the exact formula is built from exactly that; this assembles the FULL 2D Laplacian and diagonalises it, so
// agreement is a result rather than a restatement of the method. A separable solver checked against a separable
// formula would be marking its own homework.
//
// AND THE WR-90 X-BAND GUIDE COMES OUT AT 6.5571 GHz, which is the catalogue figure an engineer can look up.
//
// ---- FRONT DOORS: NINE FACELESS INSTRUMENTS DOWN TO THREE ----
// Rather than write new pages, the existing ones absorbed them, because a second page saying the same thing
// about a different four is not a front door, it is a filing decision.
//   method-lab.html took clocks, perceptual-diff, render-accountability and recon-quality -- none has a picture
//     to show, and inventing one would be worse than the absence they already record honestly.
//   beam.html took buckling, which belongs there rather than anywhere else: static asks where a loaded beam ends
//     up, vibration asks how an unloaded one rings, buckling asks when it stops being stable, and ALL THREE RUN
//     THROUGH ONE MATRIX. Putting the third key on a separate page would have hidden the only interesting thing
//     about it.
//   waveguide.html is new, because the mode SPECTRUM and the sabotage are genuinely visual: the wrong boundary
//     condition draws a line where no mode exists.
// THREE REMAIN page:null AND SHOULD: sph-hydrostatic and lbm-two-frequency each record a FAILURE as their
// finding, and skillbook is a reader.
//
// Registry 65 -> 66 instruments. Knowledge index -> 749 gates.
