// v3562 -- TORQUE-FREE RIGID BODY ROTATION: THE LAB'S FIRST KEY THAT GRADES AN EQUATION OF MOTION.
//
// A new branch. Everything before measured a field, a profile, a boundary, an exponent or a transition; this
// measures A SOLVER'S HONESTY ABOUT ITS OWN RIGHT-HAND SIDE. Euler's equations for a body with no torque on it
// are I1 w1' = (I2 - I3) w2 w3 and cyclic -- and that right-hand side IS -w x (I w), the gyroscopic term, which
// is the entire content. Without it w is CONSTANT and a body spins forever about whatever axis it was given.
//
// *** THE PLANT IS THEREFORE NOT INVENTED: GAME SOLVERS ROUTINELY DROP THAT TERM, because w x I w is stiff and
// can inject energy, and Jolt exposes it as an OPT-IN. The plant is a model of a shipping backend. ***
//
// A -- *** AND EVERY CONSERVATION KEY IS BLIND TO IT, WORSE THAN BLIND: IT RATES THE PLANT SUPERIOR. *** With the
//   term gone w is constant, so energy and |L| are conserved EXACTLY -- zero drift against the correct solver's
//   2.80e-14 of integrator error. A SOLVER THAT DELETES THE PHYSICS OUTSCORES ONE THAT KEEPS IT ON THE OBVIOUS
//   KEY. That is v3422's white-dwarf plant (where dropping the relativistic factor MADE AN EXPONENT KEY LOOK
//   BETTER) in a new subject, and it is why this module ships four key families rather than one.
//
// B -- THE ONE KEY THAT SEES IT IS THE STABILITY EXPONENT, AND IT IS A PREDICTED NUMBER RATHER THAN A SIGN.
//   Linearising about rotation at rate W gives d2(dw)/dt2 = -W^2 (Ik-Ii)(Ik-Ij)/(Ii Ij) dw: for the largest and
//   smallest axes the factors share a sign and the perturbation OSCILLATES; for the INTERMEDIATE axis they do
//   not, and it grows as exp(sigma t) with sigma = W sqrt((I2-I1)(I3-I2)/(I1 I3)). MEASURED 0.48037780 against
//   a predicted 0.48038446 -- **1.4e-5**, r2 = 0.9999999993. *** A SIGN-ONLY KEY WOULD PASS ANY SOLVER THAT IS
//   UNSTABLE FOR ANY REASON; A WRONG EQUATION GETS THE RATE WRONG EVEN WHEN IT HAPPENS TO GROW. ***
//
// C -- *** A FIT THAT STARTS AT THE SEED MEASURES A MIXTURE OF TWO MODES, AND IT DOES NOT LOOK WRONG. *** The
//   linearised solution is A e^(sigma t) + B e^(-sigma t), so near t = 0 the DECAYING mode still matters. My
//   first version fitted from the seed and read 6.89e-3 -- nearly FIVE HUNDRED TIMES further from the predicted
//   rate -- at r2 = 0.99977, which anybody would report as an excellent fit. THE GIVE-AWAY IS NOT THE RESIDUAL,
//   IT IS WHERE THE WINDOW STARTS. And tightening the SATURATION cap instead makes it WORSE (6.07e-3 -> 9.97e-3
//   as the cap falls 0.2 -> 0.002), because that keeps the transient and discards the clean part -- which is
//   how the cause was identified rather than guessed.
