// in its own header -- Householder plus implicit-shift QL -- and A COMPANION MATRIX IS NOT SYMMETRIC, so reusing
// it would have returned confident nonsense rather than an error. Durand--Kerner therefore needs its own key, and
// it is VIETA: rebuild the coefficients from the roots. A ROOT-FINDER GRADED ONLY AGAINST THE POLYNOMIAL IT WAS
// ASKED ABOUT IS A MIRROR.
//
// *** AND THE SWEEP COULD NOT CATCH THE DEFECT, WHICH IS THE ROUND. *** The sign count read
// Math.sign(col[i]) !== Math.sign(col[i-1]), and Math.sign(0) IS 0, so a ZERO ENTRY COUNTED AS A SIGN CHANGE
// AGAINST ANYTHING POSITIVE. It survived all 2800 and failed on the FIRST physically interesting case it met:
// the discrete oscillatory boundary z = -1, whose transformed polynomial has its single root AT the origin, where
// the table called one unstable root against a truth of zero-and-marginal. RANDOM COEFFICIENTS ESSENTIALLY NEVER
// PRODUCE AN EXACT ZERO, AND THE CASES THAT DO ARE THE ONES A STABILITY TEST EXISTS TO FIND. A suite of random
// polynomials would have certified it forever. A ZERO IN THE FIRST COLUMN MEANS A ROOT ON THE AXIS, WHICH IS
// NEITHER LEFT NOR RIGHT.
//
// *** A SECOND DEFECT WAS HIDING BEHIND THE FIRST AND IS WORSE. *** The bilinear accumulator is indexed in
// ASCENDING powers and routhHurwitz takes HIGHEST FIRST, and the first version handed it over unreversed -- AND
// STILL RETURNED THE RIGHT STABLE/UNSTABLE VERDICT ON EVERY ORDINARY GAIN, because reversing a polynomial maps
// its roots to their RECIPROCALS and inside-the-unit-circle is preserved under that map. IT IS WRONG EXACTLY ON
// THE CIRCLE, WHICH IS THE BOUNDARY THE FUNCTION EXISTS TO LOCATE. A convention error invisible everywhere except
// the one place the answer matters, and it was only found because the marginal case was being checked at all.
//
// THE THIRD ROUTE IS 970 KB OF SOLVER, AND v3567 LOOKED IN THE WRONG PLACE FOR IT. That round reported the
// Endless Sky autopilot as the wrong home -- combat.js stepAI is a three-valued RELAY WITH A DEADBAND feeding a
// saturating plant, and Routh--Hurwitz grades a LINEAR system -- and that reading stands. *** THE HONEST HOME WAS
// IN box3d ALL ALONG: swk_joint_weld TAKES hertz AND damping, WHICH IS s^2 + 2 zeta omega s + omega^2. *** The
// solver reproduces critical damping AS AN INTEGER: zero crossings at zeta 1.0/1.5/3.0 and 15/6/2/1 at
// 0.05/0.2/0.5/0.9. The boundary is then RECOVERED BY BISECTION ON THAT YES/NO, with zeta = 1 never mentioned to
// the solver: 0.8987 / 0.9483 / 0.9743 / 0.9807 at 1/2/4/8 Hz, the offset halving per doubling.
//
// AND IT CONVERGES UNDER dt TO 0.951 RATHER THAN TO 1 (0.9377 -> 0.9483 -> 0.9510 across a 16x refinement), so
// box3d's SOFT weld constraint's `damping` argument is not exactly the textbook zeta -- the model and not the
// integrator, v3542's rule and the v3570 friction residual a third time. THE OBVIOUS ALTERNATIVE WAS TESTED AND
// REFUTED RATHER THAN ASSUMED AWAY: a short observation window would also depress the boundary, and lifting it
// 4s -> 8s -> 16s -> 32s returns 0.898740 BIT-IDENTICALLY. Explaining a disappointing number is free; making it
