// v3583 -- POWDER RINGS AND FRIEDEL'S LAW, AND THE "BRIDGE" TO LOCKSTEP TURNS OUT TO BE A DISAMBIGUATION.
//
// *** r3(7) = 0 IS A SECOND KIND OF EXACT ZERO AND THIS LAB HAD NOT COLLECTED ONE BEFORE. *** Grind a crystal to
// powder and direction averages away, so only |G| survives and the ring is labelled by the INTEGER
// N = h^2+k^2+l^2. Seven is not a sum of three squares -- no integer of the form 4^a(8b+7) is -- so THE SIMPLE-
// CUBIC RING AT N=7 IS MISSING, AND NOT BECAUSE ANY BASIS CANCELS IT. v3579's absences come from ATOMS
// INTERFERING; this one comes from ARITHMETIC. Two different mechanisms producing the same unmissable nothing,
// in one pattern.
//
// MULTIPLICITY BY TWO ROUTES THAT SHARE NOTHING: a triple loop over hkl, against the coefficients of theta3(q)^3
// -- A CONVOLUTION OF POWER SERIES WITH NO h, k OR l ANYWHERE IN IT. 121 consecutive integers, ZERO mismatches:
// geometry against number theory. The ring sequences come out as the textbook signatures (bcc even; fcc 3, 4, 8,
// 11; diamond 3, 8, 11, 16) DERIVED FROM THE ABSENCE RULE rather than typed, and all four differ -- which is the
// one job a powder photograph exists to do.
//
// FRIEDEL'S LAW IS EXACTLY 0.000e+0 ACROSS 2916 PAIRS. Not roundoff. This lab has many keys at 1e-15 and the
// difference here is that NO ARITHMETIC HAPPENS BETWEEN THE TWO ANSWERS, only a sign: the sums are complex
// conjugates and |z| = |z-bar| bit for bit.
//
// *** AND THE OBVIOUS WAY TO BREAK IT DOES NOT WORK. *** Every account says anomalous scattering breaks Friedel.
// Put an anomalous atom into FCC and the worst difference stays at 1.8e-15: THE LAW STILL HOLDS, because FCC IS
// CENTROSYMMETRIC and an inversion centre restores the conjugate relation however complex the scattering is. IT
// TAKES BOTH CONDITIONS -- a 2x2 with THREE EXACT ZEROS and one large number:
//
//                            real f          anomalous f''=0.5
//     centrosymmetric        0.0e+0             1.8e-15
//     non-centrosymmetric    0.0e+0             2.7e+0        <- zincblende, and it breaks LOUDLY
//
// A TEST THAT HAD ONLY RUN THE FOURTH CELL WOULD HAVE CALLED THE LAW "BROKEN BY ANOMALOUS SCATTERING" AND BEEN
// WRONG ABOUT WHY. At f'' = 0.5 the classic pair reads |F(111)| = 7.211103 against 4.472136 -- a factor of 1.6,
// monotone in f''. Turning the key off IS the physics: the SIZE of the violation is how absolute structure is
// determined in a real experiment.
//
// ================================================================================================================
//
// *** AND THE LOCKSTEP BRIDGE THE REVIEW ASKED FOR IS A FALSE CONNECTION, WHICH IS THE OTHER HALF OF THE ROUND. ***
// v3579 said: v3573 proved exp(A*dt) preserves the unstable-mode count at every dt, box3dLockstep depends on that
// claim without stating it, and nothing connects the two. THE FIRST HALF IS RIGHT AND THE SECOND IS WRONG.
