//
// THE KEY: precession rate * omega must return THE APPLIED TORQUE -- a constant the measurement never sees,
// because the rate is unwrapped out of the trajectory's axis angle. 11.808, 11.938, 11.970, 11.977, 11.979
// across omega 10 to 160 against tau = 12.
//
// *** AND IT REFUSES ON ITS OWN SUBJECT MATTER. *** The law is the FAST-TOP approximation: it assumes precession
// is slow compared with spin, so it must fail when they are comparable, and it does -- 80%, 61%, 33% and 6.3%
// relative error at omega 0.5, 1, 2 and 5. An adjudicator that only rejects a NaN or a negative mass HAS NEVER
// BEEN TESTED AGAINST THE THING IT IS FOR. This one rejects omega = 2: a perfectly well-formed spin at which the
// closed form is simply not true.
//
// THE TOLERANCE IS DERIVED, NOT CHOSEN. The error does not vanish at high spin, it settles onto a floor, AND THE
// FLOOR IS THE TIMESTEP, FIRST ORDER: 3.44e-3, 1.72e-3, 4.30e-4, 1.08e-4 at dt = 1/30, 1/60, 1/240, 1/960. So
// the bound is 0.10*dt with 2x headroom STATED SEPARATELY rather than folded into the constant. Exact agreement
// would reject every correct answer -- v3570's friction offset in a new subject -- and a hand-picked 5% would
// ACCEPT omega = 5, where the law is 6.3% wrong.
//
